  "reason": "Existing evidence is sparse: RNA single-profile PCA is the best result so far (0.4849 accuracy, 0.4639 F1), while image-only ResNet is much weaker (0.2079 accuracy, 0.1718 F1). This supports exploiting the RNA direction before adding multimodal fusion. config_002 keeps the strongest known RNA encoder, pca_n2000, and tests whether moving from single-profile to multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improves performance. It is the best next experiment because it directly tests a central profile/aggregation design choice with minimal added complexity, avoids assuming that transformer aggregation or multimodality will help, and will clarify whether multiprofile RNA is worth pursuing before testing more complex configurations."
